@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
title TARGET DESIGN: Windows prompt protection subprocess
class "runGrok" as caller <<existing relay extension DESIGN>>
class "Protect-GrokPrompt.ps1" as protect <<Added DESIGN>> {
 param(OwnedDirectory : absolute path)
 validate owned directory argument
 create non-inheriting DirectorySecurity
 grant current user + SYSTEM only
 Set-Acl / verify before success
 exit nonzero on protection failure
}
class "pwsh.exe" as runtime <<external runtime>> {
 native pwsh.exe from absolute PATH entries
 -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File FIXED_SCRIPT
}
class "Invocation-local directory" as temp <<Added data>> {
 random exclusive owned path
 no prompt bytes before protection success
 parent performs write and finally cleanup
}
caller --> runtime : starts fixed helper with path only
runtime --> protect : executes shipped script
protect --> temp : apply / verify ACL
protect --> caller : exit 0 or error
note bottom of protect
Windows only. Linux uses native 0700/0600 modes.
No prompt text in argv; no dynamic command evaluation.
Protected residue may remain after an uncatchable crash.
end note
legend bottom
Added DESIGN: fixed helper and invocation-local storage.
External: existing PowerShell7 runtime.
Modified: Grok invocation calls helper before writing.
Unchanged: existing Claude/Codex behavior.
Removed/replaced: none.
endlegend
@enduml
